  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_b37e275d9ed54498992244e4d06c1603",
      "statement": "Docling runs in a spawned subprocess rather than in-process specifically so that an uncatchable out-of-memory SIGKILL becomes an observable non-zero return code in the parent instead of terminating the whole cqg run, a path pinned by a test that forces return code 137 and asserts the document still yields content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/docling_worker.py#L1-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:97d8e04e33234d105c5efff74ba78115d50ad3803c52620086887acf5fb9fb6e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/parse.py#L136-L172",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bdbc6bcc5fe18b65e73fc7b833def2dfdccc596871c8530267afa0803f8a1e1c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_parse.py#L199-L215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76301f1894cda3bd2f23ba07a34857570497d7b496269c9e8ec2cd6bc90f9ecf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95dbd2cf96c8449aab4018c9f70cff4c",
      "statement": "The docling worker exposes a minimal argv contract validated as exactly 3 or 5 arguments, treats start/end as a 1-based inclusive page range passed through as Docling's page_range, writes its markdown to a caller-supplied file rather than stdout, and converts every internal exception into a non-zero exit code.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/docling_worker.py#L1-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d0bd2f94e4edaeead0e8164c7988ed738617e1e5d30101b3e369af65782c5af:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_875dd102b402414ba299b9eeec66633a",
      "statement": "The docling worker fixes its pipeline options rather than exposing them: OCR is disabled because the target corpus is digital PDFs, table-structure recognition is enabled, and page and picture image generation are both disabled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/docling_worker.py#L21-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6acfbf8ee2d7d1581dbb950b039a3354696942f3b5181fad680a5a59a04fe2c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c691132a946a4f538bb2a4bb0e6dd2af",
      "statement": "The parent walks the document in page batches spawning a fresh subprocess per batch, accepting that models reload each time in exchange for RAM being returned to the OS on process exit, and a test confirms a three-page PDF at batch_pages=1 produces exactly three subprocess invocations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/parse.py#L128-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:848800a8f311540068cbfba652b619b07b370010307dd978efca58fea361d51d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_parse.py#L175-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73d95e6461035292c83da151405e40a621afdfe74f476ffa4b6af73450de2d91:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71c09217d8e04f7b81d611520da045a5",
      "statement": "Batch size is an operator-tunable RAM/latency tradeoff exposed as `parsing.docling_batch_pages`, defaulting to the most conservative value of one page per batch for constrained environments, with measured peak-RSS and runtime figures recorded in docs/GUIDE-run-docling-complet.md.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://config/config.example.yaml#L22-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c995e5d50b517403b55ca6bfce7c89f53c445993510b029a550c50f89f408731:"
